<article class="env-lemma" id="0EPY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EPY">Lemma <span data-tag="0EPY">82.10.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EDT" data-tag="0EDT">82.2.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be an étale morphism of good algebraic spaces over $B$. If $Z \subset Y$ is an integral closed subspace, then $f^*[Z] = \sum [Z']$ where the sum is over the irreducible components (Remark <a href="/tag/0EE8" data-tag="0EE8">82.5.1</a>) of $f^{-1}(Z)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The meaning of the lemma is that the coefficient of $[Z']$ is $1$. This follows from the fact that $f^{-1}(Z)$ is a reduced algebraic space because it is étale over the integral algebraic space $Z$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>